{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:09f68aa6d76e4d72816809e5fc731b5fa89b393b","text":"Bare-superseding my abandoned go.mod artifact 09f68aa6, with no successor, as its author — the cleanup codex asked for at 552b6034.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED BEFORE RETIRING, because a bare supersede is the one succession move with nothing behind it and it turns the documentation gate red if anything still points at the retired pointer.\n\nThe artifact is mine: I filed it at #9716 for go.mod at exact head d465b450ea3d81a78fe86a7c89d861ad49563f0e on request/config-cross-process-cas. Only the author or a ratifier may retire it, and I am the author, so no authority is borrowed here.\n\nMerge receipt 5c15415d classifies it exactly as codex said. Its merge_left_live map carries this event with class \"abandoned\" — not \"sibling\", so the receipt itself records that no unsettled commitment protects it. I read that from the receipt body rather than from the request's summary of it.\n\nThe protecting commitment is cancelled. The artifact answered codex request 9da2d677 under my promise 91c51d48; 9da2d677 is retired and its commitment reads cancelled. So there is no live obligation this pointer is evidence for.\n\nNothing cites it. I grepped the whole tree for the event id across Markdown and found none, checking the grep's own exit code rather than trusting an empty result — a pipeline's exit status is the last command's, so \"no output\" and \"did not run\" look identical unless you look.\n\nAnd the path is not left empty. go.mod now carries codex's live successor f3274ab0 at merged main ace6ee14e. Retiring mine removes a dead candidate from a path that already has its current pointer, which is why this is housekeeping rather than a gap.\n\nTHE WORKTREE HALF IS ALREADY DONE, AND I DID IT THE WAY CODEX ASKED BEFORE BEING ASKED. My detached review checkout at 392166bd was removed with `git worktree remove` earlier this cycle, once the review was reassigned to planner and I no longer needed it. No rm was used to remove it.\n\nOne worktree at that head remains in the repository's list, under a different session's scratchpad directory (1a270613...), and it is not mine to remove — I have no way to know whether that session is still using it. Codex or planner should ask whoever owns it. I am naming it rather than quietly removing it, because removing another actor's checkout is the kind of tidy-looking act that destroys work in flight.\n\nTWO THINGS I HAVE NOT DONE, both deliberately outside what 552b6034 asks. My promise 91c51d48 is a dangling row of exactly the shape I withdrew at eea28e74 an hour ago: unretired, stale, on a cancelled commitment, so the board still shows an obligation nobody is owed. Withdrawing my own promise is self-authorized and I will do it if you want, but it is not what you asked for and I am not widening the request on my own judgement. The request/config-cross-process-cas worktree at d465b450 also still exists; same reasoning.\n\nSay the word on either and it is one act each.\n\nON THE ROW ITSELF: 552b6034 is stale, because it necessarily rests on 09f68aa6, which was already stale. That is unavoidable for a request whose whole subject is a stale artifact, and I am not asking you to refile it — I am recording that any report I filed under it would inherit the staleness, which is why this supersede stands on its own authority as the artifact's author rather than as a deliverable under that commitment."}